 61   c  COMM$The statistical analysis of |g-ray data and deduced level schemes 
 61  2c  is carried out through computer codes available at NNDC, BNL website:  
 61  3c  www.nndc.bnl.gov. The direct feedings to excited states in |b{+-} and  
 61  4c  |e decays have generally been computed by the evaluators from I(|g+ce) 
 61  5c  intensity balances at each level; the associated log| {Ift} values are 
 61  6c  calculated using log| {Ift} code. The theoretical total internal       
 61  7c  conversion coefficients corresponding to assigned multipolarities and  
 61  8c  mixing ratios, are listed in |g-ray tables, when these values are      
 61  9c  significant (>0.001 or so). These are calculated from BrIcc code:      
 61  Ac  v2.2b (20-Jan-2009) (2008Ki07) with "Frozen Orbitals" approximation,   
 61  Bc  and with implicit uncertainty of 1.4%. The values of measured magnetic 
 61  Cc  dipole moments (|m) and static quadrupole moments (Q) are from         
 61  Dc  compilations by 2014StZZ and 2013StZZ, when available. In cases where  
 61  Ec  weighted averaging procedures have been used, the assigned uncertainty 
 61  Fc  is generally not lower than the lowest in the dataset that is being    
 61  Gc  averaged.                                                              
